The best approach for your .NET 10 project is **`System.IO.Abstractions`** — a well-established NuGet package that wraps `File.*`, `Directory.*`, and more behind `IFileSystem`.

### 1. Install the package

```bash
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

For your test project:
```bash
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```

### 2. Register in DI

In `Program.cs`:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

### 3. Inject `IFileSystem` into your classes

Your `ReportGenerator` currently calls `File.WriteAllText`, `Directory.Exists`, and `Directory.CreateDirectory` as bare statics. After refactoring:

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

namespace NeedsWrappers.Services;

public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
        var outputDir = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
        {
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);
        }

        var reportPath = Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_{timestamp}.txt");
        var content = $"Report: {reportName}\nGenerated: {DateTime.UtcNow:O}\nMachine: {Environment.MachineName}";

        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);
        Console.WriteLine($"Report written to {reportPath}");

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

### 4. Test with `MockFileSystem`

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers;

var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.AddDirectory("/tmp/reports");

var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
generator.GenerateReport("Sales");

// Assert the file was written
var files = mockFs.Directory.GetFiles("/tmp/reports");
Assert.Single(files);
Assert.Contains("Sales_", files[0]);
```

### Bonus: other statics in that file

Your `ReportGenerator` also has `DateTime.UtcNow`, `Environment.*`, and `Console.WriteLine`. For a fully testable class:

| Static | Recommended abstraction |
|---|---|
| `DateTime.UtcNow` | Built-in `TimeProvider` (inject + `FakeTimeProvider` in tests) |
| `Environment.*` | Custom `IEnvironmentProvider` wrapper |
| `Console.WriteLine` | Custom `IConsole` wrapper (or just ignore if logging-only) |

Want me to generate wrappers for any of those too?
